{"availability":"available","full":"lokutor-ai/ito","name":"ito","description":"Natural-sounding streaming text-to-speech for the ESP32-S3: 4.4 M params, 4.9 MB, no cloud, no NPU","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"C","stars":18,"forks":1,"created":"2026-10-02T14:45:34Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:07:16Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","topics":["edge-ai","embedded","esp32","esp32-s3","microcontroller","speech-synthesis","streaming","text-to-speech","tinyml","tts"],"demo":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:24:23.024Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:24:23.024Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:24:23.024Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","stars":5,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:31:26.142Z","stars":11,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:09:09.086Z","stars":16,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-11T07:24:23.024Z","stars":18,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ito is English text-to-speech whose neural model runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. Phonemization runs on the host in this release: a computer turns the text into phoneme ids (espeak-ng) and sends them to the chip over serial, so on the chip Ito goes from phoneme ids to waveform, and every time below starts at the ids. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (125 ms of audio) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS…","First run on a physical board (8 October 2026): the first public prebuilt image crash-looped on first boot on real hardware: its GDMA self-test overflowed a heap buffer, which QEMU cannot show. That run found four first-silicon bugs (the GDMA self-test heap overflow, bench scratch fragmentation, underrun accounting, USB console input), fixed in fedbd26 (with the notes in e196730). The prebuilt image in this repository is the fixed one, and the logs of the crashing runs are kept in esp32/logs/boardcrash.log. The measured numbers below come from the fixed image. Status (9 October 2026). The…","Stability on the board (9 October 2026). Same board and firmware (fedbd26), 240 MHz, female voice, USB powered, nothing attached, I2S idle. Soak: each iteration runs the boot golden sentence in three modes (dual-core 8-bit, single-core, dual-core 16-bit) and compares the output hash with the host C engine. Main int8 set: 300 iterations (900 runs, all PASS, 0 FAIL, 78 minutes; hashes 023bd6b1 and 9666bb9e, identical to the host C engine). Int4 set: 100 iterations (300 PASS, 0 FAIL; host hash 363d7d98). Light set: 100 iterations (300 PASS, 0 FAIL; 5f12d5e1). Main int8 set again with I2S idle:…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"48e40fc886ed1eafd1028c6ee6bcbc2ebb2d4add435eb12af94153d023b87b6e","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T04:09:04.405Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T04:09:04.405Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ito is English text-to-speech whose neural model runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. Phonemization runs on the host in this release: a computer turns the text into phoneme ids (espeak-ng) and sends them to the chip over serial, so on the chip Ito goes from phoneme ids to waveform, and every time below starts at the ids. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (125 ms of audio) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":